IMPORT prelude

-- Industrial Relations Act 1960 (Singapore) -- what a union may bargain over (s 18(2)), the term of a collective agreement and its
-- survival on a transfer of undertaking (s 23(5), (6)), the limited representation of executives (s 30A), and dismissal: the
-- Industrial Arbitration Court's bar and the Minister's reinstatement route (s 35).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/IRA1960.txt (amendments to
-- Act 30 of 2024, which added the platform work Parts).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 13 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to bargaining limits and dismissal.
-- Not encoded: the Industrial Arbitration Court's constitution, recognition procedure, conciliation, tripartite mediation (Part 4A),
-- awards beyond s 35, the platform work Parts, and offences.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Industrial Relations Act 1960 -- bargaining`

§§ `18(2) -- matters a union may not put on the table`

-- s 18(2): "no trade union of employees may include in a notice setting out proposals for a collective agreement a proposal in
-- relation to": (a) PROMOTION; (b) TRANSFER within the organisation that is not to the employee's detriment; (c) whom the employer
-- appoints to a vacancy; (d) termination for REDUNDANCY or reorganisation "or the criteria for such termination"; (e) dismissal and
-- reinstatement (which go to the Minister under s 35(3)); (f) assignment of duties consistent with the contract.
DECLARE Proposal IS ONE OF
    `wage increases`
    `annual leave`
    `retrenchment benefits`
    `the criteria for choosing whom to retrench`
    `promotion criteria`
    `a detrimental transfer`
    `a transfer with no detriment`
    `who is hired into a vacancy`
    `assignment of duties within the contract`

GIVEN `the proposal` IS A Proposal
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the union may propose it` IF
    CONSIDER `the proposal`
    WHEN `the criteria for choosing whom to retrench` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `promotion criteria` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a transfer with no detriment` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `who is hired into a vacancy` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `assignment of duties within the contract` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `23(5), (6) -- the collective agreement`

-- s 23(5)(a): a collective agreement must run "not less than 2 years or more than 3 years".
-- (6): on a transfer of undertaking under the Employment Act s 18A, the agreement continues with the transferee "for a period of 18
-- months after the date of the transfer or until the date of its expiry ..., whichever is the LATER".
GIVEN `years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the term is valid` IF
    `years` AT LEAST 2 AND `years` AT MOST 3

GIVEN `months of the agreement remaining at transfer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`months the agreement binds the transferee` MEANS
    IF `months of the agreement remaining at transfer` GREATER THAN 18 THEN `months of the agreement remaining at transfer` ELSE 18

§§ `30A -- executives`

-- s 30A(1): a union may represent an executive "individually, and not as a class", and only to (a) seek reinstatement from the
-- Minister, (b) resolve a retrenchment-benefit dispute, (c) resolve a breach-of-contract dispute, (d) appear in victimisation
-- proceedings, (e) resolve a re-employment dispute. (2): the employer may object only on the ground that the executive is in senior
-- management (or similar).
DECLARE ExecMatter IS ONE OF
    `seeking reinstatement after dismissal`
    `a retrenchment benefit dispute`
    `a breach of contract dispute`
    `a re-employment dispute`
    `a collective pay claim for all executives`

GIVEN `the matter` IS AN ExecMatter, `is senior management` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the union may represent the executive` IF
        (NOT `is senior management`)
    AND CONSIDER `the matter`
        WHEN `a collective pay claim for all executives` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `35 -- dismissal`

-- s 35(2): the Industrial Arbitration Court "shall not consider a dispute relating to the dismissal of an employee or make an award
-- relating to the reinstatement" except for victimisation under s 82.
-- (3): an employee who considers the dismissal without just cause may, "within ONE MONTH", make representations THROUGH THEIR TRADE
-- UNION to the Minister. (6): if satisfied, the Minister may direct reinstatement with back wages, or compensation. (8): the decision
-- is "final and conclusive and shall not be challenged in any court". (9): a direction "shall operate as a BAR to any action for
-- damages by the employee in any court in respect of the wrongful dismissal". (10): an employer who does not comply -- $10,000 or 12
-- months.
GIVEN `months since dismissal` IS A NUMBER, `through the union` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the representations are in time and in form` IF
    `months since dismissal` AT MOST 1 AND `through the union`

GIVEN `the Minister gave a direction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee may still sue for wrongful dismissal` IF
    NOT `the Minister gave a direction`

GIVEN `victimisation for union activity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Arbitration Court may hear the dismissal` IF
    `victimisation for union activity`
